127
00:09:03,960 --> 00:09:08,960
He has a very good analogy in it. It's called dish washing.

128
00:09:09,540 --> 00:09:16,120
Dish washing is how many dishes you wash.

129
00:09:16,200 --> 00:09:21,880
For example, if you have eaten rice and lentils, how many plates do you have to wash?

130
00:09:21,960 --> 00:09:23,340
Only one, right?

131
00:09:23,760 --> 00:09:32,207
But if you think about all the plates that you washed before and all the plates that you will wash after in future,

132
00:09:32,287 --> 00:09:35,900
that would look like a Burj Khalifa of dishes, right?

133
00:09:37,110 --> 00:09:43,610
You will see a huge difference in the dishes and you will be demotivated.

134
00:09:43,690 --> 00:09:48,170
So life should be like dishwashing.

135
00:09:48,250 --> 00:09:50,970
Today you have to wash only one dish.

136
00:09:51,050 --> 00:09:53,470
So focus on today.

137
00:09:53,550 --> 00:09:55,230
Forget the dishes in the past.

138
00:09:55,310 --> 00:09:57,130
When the next one is dirty, you will wash it too.

139
00:09:57,210 --> 00:09:58,690
But you have to wash only one dish.

140
00:09:58,770 --> 00:10:00,090
You have to wash only one dish in a day.

141
00:10:00,170 --> 00:10:02,890
So take life one step at a time, one day at a time.

142
00:10:02,970 --> 00:10:03,880
So wash today's plate.

143
00:10:03,960 --> 00:10:07,881
Today's plate is washed, so I understand that due to weight issues,

144
00:10:07,961 --> 00:10:13,090
you have a physical limitation and you have washed the pedestrian plate perfectly.

145
